    kind: work_item  # 88bf
    title: "Python shape_id collapses different-kind symbols (class/method/function) and mis-hashes async def — node kind + AsyncFunctionDef absent from hash inputs"  # 88bf
    status: todo_hard  # 88bf
    priority: 1  # 88bf
    parent:  # 88bf
    tags:  # 88bf
    - dogfood  # 88bf
    isbefore: []  # 88bf
    duplicate_of: []  # 88bf
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 88bf
    pr_ref:  # 88bf
    description: "**Mechanism.** Python shape_id (structural-implementation fingerprint, spec §337/§342, \"changes if control flow changed\") omits the node KIND from its hash inputs, and `_compute_shape_id` (py.py:1649) tests `isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef | ast.ClassDef)` — but `ast.AsyncFunctionDef` is NOT a subclass of `ast.FunctionDef`, so async defs are hashed via the ClassDef branch. Net effect: a docstring-only class, a sync method, and an async method with byte-identical body structure all get the SAME shape_id.\n\n**Evidence (frozen substrate a32c4a31).** 61 distinct shape_ids span >1 node kind; 689 nodes sit in mixed-kind clusters (59 `('function','method')`, 2 `('class','method')`). Cleanest group `sha256:44283d00f7d29138` (17 nodes) = 16 docstring-only Exception classes + 1 async method (`NullDuressHandler.on_duress_login`, serve_duress.py:82). FRESH-RUN REPRODUCED on /tmp: a docstring-only `class FooError(Exception)` and an `async def on_event` produced the same shape_id, byte-matching the substrate; `def plain_func()` and `def plain_method(self)` also collide.\n\n**Two sub-fixes (a fixer may split):** (1) include node kind in the shape hash inputs (fixes function/method/class conflation); (2) add `ast.AsyncFunctionDef` to the isinstance check (fixes async mis-hashing). \n\n**Consequence.** A consumer (human or LLM agent) using shape_id for clone-detection / \"find structurally-identical implementations\" gets false groupings conflating classes with methods and sync with async defs; an agent could propose dedup/refactor across genuinely different-kind symbols. Blind-judged Significant (sev 4).\n\n**Distinct from:** WI-lutob (shape_id=None on csharp/solidity/wgsl body-bearing), WI-luzut (shape_id=null on Python variables), WI-tisar (stable_id/shape_id share sha256: prefix). This is the only item about cross-KIND value COLLISION. Source: dogfood tranche-08 F157.A1 — recovered post-judging (a Phase-3a CORRECTION-of-a-POSITIVE mis-classification had dropped it from carding; reclassified INDEPENDENT and blind-judged sev 4)."  # 88bf
    fields: {}  # 88bf
